     1	"""System B — the set-off / run primitive. "Run step N of ticket X": assemble the
     2	role env, drive W1's ``run_step`` (spawn a gateway child, create/resume the mind,
     3	submit one prompt, observe the single run-end), run the proposal-present invariant,
     4	and write the ticket's run-status. System B is the SOLE writer of ``tickets.status``
     5	(→ notes.md Principles: "code owns all state stamps; agents propose, one door writes").
     6	
     7	Serialization — keyed on ``ticket_id`` (the STABLE per-mind identity):
     8	  One mind == one ticket, so every run of a ticket must be serialized (at most one
     9	  in-flight) and must resume the mind's CURRENT durable ``session_key``. The durable
    10	  key is NOT a stable identity — the gateway auto-compresses and ROTATES it mid-run
    11	  (spike 01: resume then follows the rotation chain to the live tip). Keying the
    12	  ``MindQueue`` on the rotating key value would split one mind across two keys and let
    13	  two children resume it concurrently, defeating the gateway's per-process busy-guard
    14	  (the very hazard the queue exists to prevent). So the queue is keyed on ``ticket_id``
    15	  (its "one in-flight per key" property maps exactly to "one in-flight run per mind"),
    16	  and the current ``session_key`` is resolved from the DB at EXECUTION time inside the
    17	  serialized run.
    18	
    19	  This also subsumes W1's "System B must serialize kickoff itself": step-0 (no key
    20	  yet) and step-N of the same ticket share the ``ticket_id`` key, so the queue
    21	  serializes them; the run resolves ``None`` -> ``session.create`` (kickoff) and stores
    22	  the created key, and the next run resolves it -> ``session.resume``. Two step-0 runs
    23	  never both create.
    24	
    25	Kickoff = step 0 through the same ``run_step`` call. ``errored`` stops and surfaces
    26	(no auto-retry). System B is not wired into the running server in W3a — System A (the
    27	readiness poll that calls ``set_off``) is W3b; this is exercised by unit tests against
    28	``minds/fake.py``."""
